vtest "cachetag default limits pass real 333-tag objects and fail closed at 512"

# Review 20260718_0852 section 5: production traces carry up to 333 tags on
# one object. The default max_keys_per_object (512) must accept them on the
# unconfigured path, accept exactly 512, and fail the fetch (503, fail
# closed) at 513. The purge path must accept a 333-token purge header (the
# former independent 256-token ceiling is removed) and stale() must reject
# the purged 333-tag object before delivery.

